    "media:imagetext": "\"GOLDEN GATE INTERNATIONAL EXPOSITION\"\nThis is the first official view of the Golden Gate Inter-\nnational Exposition Island,\nas it will appear in 1939\nThe view is from the shore of Yerba Buena Island, look-\ning north.\nIn the immediate leit loreground is a l10-foot cause-\nway, serving\na boulevard approach from the San\nFrancisco-Oakland Bay Bridge.\nAt the right is Exposi-\ntion Harbor,\n1500 feet wide and 3400 feet long, which\nwill be used for marine regattas.\nThe Exposition\nAdministration building\nwhich will\nserve as a future Airport Terminal, is the first building\nto the right of the roadway. The main entrance to the\nExposition is half-way up the boulevard, with the Expo-\nterminal beyond.\nTo the extreme\nright are two airport hangars which\nwill serve as exhibit palaces, and behind the hangars is\nthe Lake of All Nations. Central unit of the two major\nExes it one erosion exhibit pales is the 350e by\nthe painting, made by\nChesley Bonestell, Berkeley artist.\nPOST CARD\nTHIS SPACE FOR ADDRESS ONLY\nPLACE\nCNE CENT\nSTAMP\nHERE",
